<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apuan Alps</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Apuan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> are a mountain range in north-western Tuscany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, running parallel to the coast between the valleys of the Serchio and the Magra. Their marble, quarried around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a> since Roman times, includes the white statuary marble used by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> and many other sculptors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/apuan-alps.jpg" alt="Apuan Alps" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Ilario assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alpi_Apuane.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
